{"text": "eighteen", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">eightetene</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">ei\u021dtene</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">ehtetene</i>, from Old English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">eahtat\u012bene</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">eahtat\u0113ne</i>, from Proto-Germanic <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"gem-pro\">*aht\u014dutehun</i>. Cognate with West Frisian <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fy\">achttjin</i>, Dutch <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"nl\">achttien</i>, German <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"de\">achtzehn</i>, Danish <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"da\">atten</i>.\n</p><p>Equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">eight</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-teen</i>\n</p>", "pos": []}], "pronunciation": [["General American", "/\u02cce\u026a(t)\u02c8tin/"], ["General American", "/\u02c8e\u026a(t).tin/"]]}